# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only. Set these as Vercel Environment Variables (Production +
# Preview). They are read by api/submit-quote.ts (a Vercel Edge Function) and
# are NEVER exposed to the client bundle — they have no VITE_ prefix, so Vite
# cannot inline them. Do not commit real values; this file documents NAMES only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GHL_API_KEY=
GHL_LOCATION_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side: absolute URL of the deployed /api/submit-quote function (see
# src/lib/ghlAdapter.ts).
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET for the current architecture. As of the Vercel domain
# cutover, cleaningbykandi.com is served by Vercel itself, so the frontend and
# /api/submit-quote share one origin and ghlAdapter's relative-path fallback
# ('/api/submit-quote') is correct. Setting it is only necessary if the bundle
# is again embedded on a DIFFERENT origin (e.g. a GoHighLevel funnel page
# loading assets/cbk.js), where a relative path would resolve against that
# other origin and 404. In that case set it to the absolute function URL, e.g.
# https://cleaningbykandi.com/api/submit-quote — and note api/submit-quote.ts
# only allows CORS from https://cleaningbykandi.com, so any additional
# embedding origin must be added to that allowlist too.
#
# Exposed to the client bundle (Vite's VITE_ prefix) — never put secrets here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_QUOTE_API_URL=
